id: pm-gh1670
title: "GH-1670: pm health --full --summary silently drops --summary and emits the full projection (15.7 KB vs 636 B) with no receipt"
description: "GitHub issue #1670 (reported 2026-11-05 against 2026.11.4 from a fleet health gate run on pm-graph). Reproduced 2026-11-05 on main (e268c5b92, the 2026.11.5 cut) in a disposable one-item tracker: pm health --summary emits 636 B, while pm health --full --summary, pm health --summary --full and pm health --full each emit 15,704 B, all exit 0. Flag order does not matter and nothing in the output says the summary projection was dropped. Cause: runHealthAction in src/cli/register-operations.ts passes both summary and full to runHealth, and the full projection wins. The --full help text says it runs all checks including slow integrity, drift and vectorization, while the --strict-exit help says --full gives complete details, so one flag carries two meanings: check scope and output projection. Expected: an explicit --summary with --full runs the full check set and renders the compact summary of it (run everything, read little), which is what agents and CI gates ask for; or the combination is refused with a remedy. Never a silent drop. --strict-exit, which only implies summary, keeps its documented behaviour that --full restores complete details. Why it matters for agents: a strict gate that asks for the summary pays about 11k extra tokens per call (43.9 KB at bytes/4 on the reporter's 113-item tracker) with no omission receipt. Duplicate check: searched health summary, full, projection and flag precedence across all statuses. pm-nbht (closed) added the one-line summary mode, pm-gh1486 (closed) made passing diagnostics concise by default and pm-yjub (closed) made MCP pm_health default to the summary; none owns the precedence between --full and --summary."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 2
tags[5]: agent-ux,cli,"gh:1670",health,token-efficiency
created_at: "2026-11-05T20:47:58.374Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-06T01:23:44.813Z"
closed_at: "2026-11-06T00:37:26.520Z"
completed_at: "2026-11-06T00:37:26.520Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 90
acceptance_criteria: "pm health --full --summary runs the full check set (integrity, drift and vectorization included) and emits the summary projection, proven by a spec that compares its bytes and check names with --summary and --full on the same tracker in CLI, SDK and MCP; pm health --strict-exit --full keeps its documented complete-details output, because strict-exit only implies summary, and help text for --full and --summary states the precedence; Negative control: restoring the full projection for an explicit --summary fails the spec"
parent: pm-5t33or
risk: low
confidence: high
severity: medium
repro_steps: "In a fresh tracker: pm health --summary | wc -c (636), pm health --full --summary | wc -c (15704), pm health --summary --full | wc -c (15704), pm health --full | wc -c (15704); all exit 0"
resolution: "For health, --full overrides the check-only fast path and the skip flags so every check runs, and its complete-details projection is now only the default. resolveHealthSkipPolicy keeps an explicit summary in summaryMode with full set. selectHealthProjection picks summary, then brief, then full. runHealthAction derives the strict-exit summary only when --full is absent. The help for --summary and --full states the precedence within the ratcheted 485-token help budget, and OUTPUT_PROJECTION_CONTRACTS.md records why health composes these flags while list, graph and deps refuse them. Proven by an integration spec over the CLI, SDK client and MCP runAction on one tracker, by projection-contract and register-commands specs, and by a negative control: reverting the source fails five assertions."
expected_result: An explicit --summary with --full runs every check and renders the compact summary; --strict-exit --full keeps complete details
actual_result: "--full --summary and --summary --full return mode summary with omitted_checks empty and the same check names as --full; --check-only --full --summary runs integrity, history_drift and vectorization; --strict-exit --full returns complete details; full suite 12072 passed with 100/100/100/100 coverage"
affected_version: 2026.11.4
component: health
